# The empirical evaluation lives on the `eval-phase1` branch and is deliberately
# never merged here - this repo is public, and eval/pilot/ contains internal
# data from a private repo used as one of the test corpora. See
# eval/PLAN.md ("Publication constraint") on that branch.
#
# Ignoring it on `main` only affects `main`: an ignore rule cannot hide files
# git already tracks, so the eval branch is unaffected. Without this, switching
# to `main` leaves ~28k untracked files behind (venvs, clones, caches that were
# never tracked on any branch) and `git status` reports a bare `?? eval/` that
# looks like uncommitted work but is not.
eval/